SUMMARY:Clocks spring forward one hour
DESCRIPTION:Daylight saving time starts at 2 a.m.\, so clocks jump to 3 a.
 m. and you lose an hour of sleep. Hawaii and most of Arizona don't change
 .\nMore: https://www.nist.gov/pml/time-and-frequency-division/popular-lin
 ks/daylight-saving-time-dst\nFrom The Civic Forecast: https://civic-forec
 ast.pages.dev
